\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the proposed attribute-guided H-CAST framework. The H-CAST backbone extracts hierarchical visual representations from the input image. Attribute-group queries attend to species-level graph-node features and produce attribute-oriented representations. These representations are supervised by group-specific attribute prediction heads and fused with the species-level class token for final species prediction. Family and order predictions are produced from the original H-CAST hierarchy. Attribute labels are used only during training.}}{30}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:proposed_overview}{{3.1}{30}{Overview of the proposed attribute-guided H-CAST framework. The H-CAST backbone extracts hierarchical visual representations from the input image. Attribute-group queries attend to species-level graph-node features and produce attribute-oriented representations. These representations are supervised by group-specific attribute prediction heads and fused with the species-level class token for final species prediction. Family and order predictions are produced from the original H-CAST hierarchy. Attribute labels are used only during training}{figure.caption.2}{}}
