\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Representative limitation case for high-weight global morphology groups. From left to right, the figure shows the original image, the spatial attention map of \textit  {shape}, the spatial attention map of \textit  {size}, and the spatial attention map of \textit  {back pattern}. In this example, the \textit  {shape} and \textit  {size} queries place substantial attention on background regions. This indicates that these maps should be interpreted as diagnostic internal attention patterns rather than ground-truth localization of size or shape.}}{88}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:size_shape_background_example}{{4.3}{88}{Representative limitation case for high-weight global morphology groups. From left to right, the figure shows the original image, the spatial attention map of \textit {shape}, the spatial attention map of \textit {size}, and the spatial attention map of \textit {back pattern}. In this example, the \textit {shape} and \textit {size} queries place substantial attention on background regions. This indicates that these maps should be interpreted as diagnostic internal attention patterns rather than ground-truth localization of size or shape}{figure.caption.16}{}}
